    "narrative": "Our lineup optimization for May 22nd prioritizes high-upside matchups against favorable arms, with **Corbin Carroll** standing out as the absolute anchor of our offense. With a projection of 85.94, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-run-environment park and a matchup against Sugano; his ability to exploit a slow pitcher delivery makes him our top stolen base threat today. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (70.26) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.05) project as elite starts, both facing pitchers with xERAs near 5.00. **James Wood** (66.78) rounds out the top tier, as his leadoff spot and stolen base potential against Elder provide a high floor that makes him an essential component of our daily scoring strategy.\n\nThe decision to bench **Dalton Rushing** (38.21) was the most difficult call of the morning, as his metrics fell just short of our 40.0 floor. While **Dalton Rushing** maintains value, his matchup against a stingy pitcher like Henderson combined with an unfavorable 8th-order slot dragged his efficiency down relative to the high-upside profiles of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Zach McKinstry**, the latter of whom received a massive 16% park boost that solidified his starting spot. Elsewhere, we are leaning into the speed-first profile of **Brice Turang** (52.00) despite the left-on-left disadvantage; his base-stealing opportunity against Wrobleski remains too valuable to ignore in our quest to win the category. We continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story**, who remains on the IL, while keeping **Josh Naylor** benched as we await official confirmation of his status. No major weather concerns are currently impacting play, but we are keeping a close eye on **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who faces the stiffest test of the day against Gilbert\u2019s 3.03 xERA; we are starting him for his order position, but acknowledge the risk of limited production against elite pitching.",
